{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    Returns string representation after the conversion using repeated division.\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    digits = []\n    while x > 0:\n        remainder = x % base\n        digits.append(str(remainder))\n        x //= base\n    \n    digits.reverse()\n    return \"\".join(digits)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "import itertools\n\ndef _validate_input(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates if the input list has at least three elements.\"\"\"\n    return len(l) >= 3\n\ndef _generate_triplets(l: list) -> itertools.combinations:\n    \"\"\"Generates all distinct triplet index combinations for the list.\"\"\"\n    return itertools.combinations(range(len(l)), 3)\n\ndef _calculate_sum(l: list, indices: tuple) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements at the given indices in the list.\"\"\"\n    return l[indices[0]] + l[indices[1]] + l[indices[2]]\n\ndef triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n\n    >>> triples_sum_to_zero([1, 3, 5, 0])\n    False\n    >>> triples_sum_to_zero([1, 3, -2, 1])\n    True\n    >>> triples_sum_to_zero([1, 2, 3, 7])\n    False\n    >>> triples_sum_to_zero([2, 4, -5, 3, 9, 7])\n    True\n    >>> triples_sum_to_zero([1])\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_input(l):\n        return False\n\n    for i, j, k in _generate_triplets(l):\n        if _calculate_sum(l, (i, j, k)) == 0:\n            return True\n\n    return False"}
